haplo-dialog, Announcements for users
======================================

This file summarises the important changes from the user's point of view.
For the complete technical history, see CHANGELOG.md.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.1.1 (2026-08-27), Fixes
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

The two ports finally install side by side: both shipped the same manual page,
and dpkg refused the second one — while the documentation promised the opposite.

That page was also wrong: it described the Wayland anchoring as working in both
ports, when only the GTK 3 one has it. The GTK 4 port now has its own page,
which says what it actually does.

The shipped examples called commands the packages do not provide. They now call
their own port's binary.

Also: the manual pages follow the version instead of staying frozen;
"make install" no longer overwrites an already installed gtkdialog; "--version"
prints a single number; a <spinbutton> in the GTK 4 port no longer prints two
warnings on every open; and the test suite no longer returns a silent success
when it finds no binary.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.1.0 (2026-08-26), Both ports on a single number
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

The packages carried two numbers to read — gtk3sermo 1.0.0-11 and gtk4sermo
1.0.0-12. They are all on 1.1.1 now, and there is only one thing to read.

This version brings the info manuals ("info gtk3sermo" finally opens
something), the --do option, the optional HAPLO_ALLOWED_CMDS bound, and ten
behaviours the program has always had with nothing documenting them.

It fixes three serious defects: the output handed to the shell could be executed
by eval if whoever used the dialog typed $(command) into a field, clicking a
<switch> killed the program, and under a French locale a number written with a
dot silently read as zero.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.0.0 (2026-05-29), First public release
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

haplo-dialog 1.0.0 is the first stable public release.

haplo-dialog is a modern, hardened and maintained descendant of gtkdialog.
It is not the only one: Mick Amadio's BunsenLabs fork also ports gtkdialog
to GTK 3, and upstream carries on at woof-CE.
Describe an interface in XML, run it from the shell, retrieve the values
entered. Where gtkdialog is abandoned, haplo-dialog brings it back to life:
fixed, hardened, maintained.

* Two ports: gtk3sermo (GTK 3 backend, the reference) and gtk4sermo
  (GTK 4 backend). The reference port implements
  43 widgets and is driven entirely in XML from the shell.

* gtkdialog backwards compatibility: installing gtk3sermo creates a
  "gtkdialog" alias, your legacy gtkdialog 0.8.x scripts run as is
  (XML, options and environment variables).

* Strengthened security: all commands go through safe_exec.
  No more direct calls to system() in the code. The parser cleanly rejects
  malformed XML, and the code is subjected to fuzzing.

* Binary hardening: _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
  stack-protector-strong, -fcf-protection (depending on the compiler).

* Test suite: 55 XML regression cases and 9 behaviour tests (safe_exec).

* .deb package built and checked for every version. Recipes provided, not
  built by us, for RPM, Arch, Gentoo and Slackware.

To install:

  # The packages are attached to the v1.1.1 release, with their checksums.
  # There is NO APT repository: you download, you verify, you install.
  sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
  sudo apt install ./gtk3sermo_1.1.2-1_amd64.deb
  # To build them yourself from a clone:
  #   cd sermo/gtk3sermo/gtk3sermo_1.1.0 && dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
  # (The resulting packages are gtk3sermo, gtksermo and gtk4sermo.
  #  The « gtkdialog » command lives in gtksermo, a separate package,
  #  deliberately in conflict with BunsenLabs' gtk3dialog.)

  # Arch Linux (recipe provided, never built by us)
  cd gtk3sermo/gtk3sermo_1.1.0/packaging/arch && makepkg -si

  # From source (autotools)
  cd gtk3sermo/gtk3sermo_1.1.0 && autoreconf -fi && ./configure && make && sudo make install

Documentation: https://haplo-dialog.fr
Bug reports: devel@haplo-dialog.fr
Security: devel@haplo-dialog.fr

──────────────────────────────────────────────────

